From fe3e9f5185e2303a30e0dd41962d367f069683f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:54:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] feat(mcp,core): default server instructions;
 descriptions say how apply, patch and charts work (C29, C16)

The server sent no instructions (server_instructions is empty by
default), and resources_create_or_update's description prescribed the
recipe that lost an update on the native session: "fetch it with
resources_get, modify it, then re-apply the full resource". Other
descriptions left out what agents then guessed: that local chart paths
work for helm_install, and that events_list takes a namespace although
it said "from all namespaces".

Server instructions (C29): when server_instructions is not configured
and the core toolset is enabled, the server sends five short notes
(about 150 tokens): the apply is not forced and should carry only the
fields to set; resources_patch for one-field edits and removals, with
resourceVersion; namespace-less objects go to the configured
namespace; receipts and output: full, pending deletes and wait;
auth_can_i and empty lists. A configured server_instructions replaces
them, as before; without core nothing is sent.

Descriptions (C16):
- resources_create_or_update: send only the fields you mean to set,
  what happens to fields you leave out and to fields other writers own,
  the upsert and mode: create, resourceVersion as a precondition,
  resources_patch for removals, the namespace default; the `resource`
  argument no longer asks for "the full spec";
- helm_install `chart`: repository charts, OCI or HTTPS URLs, and local
  chart directories or .tgz files on the server's host;
- events_list: one namespace or all.

TestServerInstructionsEmpty asserted empty instructions by default; it
is replaced by a test of the default notes and one that checks no
notes are sent without the core toolset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
